    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d333-a1">

                <pb facs="0581" n="567" sameAs="frus:frus1944v01/pg567"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Enclosure]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Director of the Office of Strategic
                        Services</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Donovan</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-12-11">11 December,
                        1944</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>In order to weaken the resistance of the German civilian population, it is
                    proposed to disseminate both by radio and by pamphlet the theme set forth in the
                    inclosed paper entitled “Black Propaganda Treatment of Unconditional
                    Surrender”.</p>
                <p>I think you understand that this material will be purported to come from within
                    Germany itself and will represent the dissatisfaction of the purported group
                    with the needless sacrifice of continued resistance.</p>
                <p>I am anxious to submit this to the Joint Chiefs of Staff but before doing so, I
                    would appreciate your concurrence as to the advisability of the attack and the
                    method proposed.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">William</hi> J. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Donovan</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
